  "text": " OutlineInputBorder\n.createSequentialGroup\n\t\t \t.text(tl(flat_list,\nublisher)\nf.append(v)\nfWithContents\nczęsto\n\n主持召开\n\n a解决方案\n\n.WriteLine\n tableLayoutPanel1\nQuestion: \nFind the least positive value of \\( t \\) such that \n\\[\n\\arccos (\\cos \\alpha), \\ \\arccos (\\cos 3 \\alpha), \\ \\arccos (\\cos 11 \\alpha), \\ \\arccos (\\cos t \\alpha)\n\\]\nis an arithmetic progression for some \\(\\alpha\\) with \\(0 < \\alpha < \\pi\\).\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n1. **Understanding the Expression for \\(\\arccos\\) of \\(\\cos\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\arccos(\\cos(\\beta))^2 = 2\\beta\n   \\]\n   Remark: For \\(0 \\leq \\beta \\leq \\pi\\), \\(\\arccos(\\cos(2\\beta))\\) is defined as the inverse cosine of \\(\\cos(2\\beta)\\), which means \\(\\arccos(\\cos(\\beta)) = \\beta\\) if \\(\\beta\\) is contained within the range \\(0 \\leq \\beta \\leq \\pi\\). For values outside this range, we subtract or add multiples of \\(2\\pi\\) to find the equivalent angle within the \\(0 \\leq \\beta \\leq \\pi\\) range.\n\n   Applying this:\n   \\[\n   \\arccos(\\cos(\\alpha)) = \\alpha\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\arccos(\\cos(3\\alpha)) = \\beta\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\arccos(\\cos(11\\alpha)) = \\gamma\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\arccos(\\cos(t\\alpha)) = \\delta\n   \\]\n\n2. **Formulating the Arithmetic Progression:**\n   The condition for four terms to be in the arithmetic progression is:\n   \\[\n   \\arccos(\\cos(3\\alpha)) - \\arccos(\\cos(\\alpha)) = \\arccos(\\cos(11\\alpha)) - \\arccos(\\cos(3\\alpha)) = \\arccos(\\cos(t\\alpha)) - \\arccos(\\cos(11\\alpha))\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determining Relationships:**\n   Let's equate the differences:\n   \\[\n   \\alpha - \\beta = \\beta - \\gamma = \\gamma - \\delta\n   \\]\n\n   Designating these common differences sum \\(r\\):\n   \\[\n   \\alpha - \\beta = r\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\beta - \\gamma = r\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\gamma - \\delta = r\n   \\]\n\n   Multiplying the expressions:\n   \\[\n   (\\alpha - \\beta)(\\gamma - \\delta)(\\beta - \\gamma) = r^3\n   \\]\n\n4. **Substituting Trigonometric Relationships:**\n   Finding relationship:\n   \\[\n   \\arccos(\\cos(3\\alpha)) - \\arccos(\\cos(\\alpha)) = \\alpha\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\alpha - \\beta = r\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\beta - \\gamma = r\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\gamma - \\delta = r\n   \\]\n\n   Reorganizing these, we substitute:\n   \\[\n   \\beta = \\alpha - r\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (\\gamma - \\alpha) = 2r\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (t \\alpha - (11 \\alpha - 4)) - r = 4\\alpha (11-4) = 6\\alpha\n   \\]\n\n5. **Solving for \\(\\alpha\\) and \\(\\delta\\):**\n   Since:\n   \\[\n   \\arccos(\\cos(3\\alpha)) = \\sin(3 \\alpha)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\arccos(\\cos(t \\alpha)) = \\sin(t \\alpha)\n   \\]\n\n6. **Final Equations Simplifying:**\n   \\[\n   \\alpha = 2\\alpha\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (\\alpha - \\beta) = \\frac{\\alpha (9)}{\\cos(9 \\alpha)}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (9 \\alpha) = (10 \\alpha)\n   \\]\n\nConclusion:\n\\[\n\\boxed{6}\n\\]",
